# Forest spider (#328, D102): native 32x16 frames, facing right, feet on row 15. Eight legs, each root -> high knee -> foot,
# all rooted on the cephalothorax and drawn behind the body: four near (l, knees L) and four far (n).
# crawl1, crawl2: the skitter; rise, tap: the notice (up on its legs, a foreleg drums); crouch: the wind-up (forelegs up,
# fangs open); leap: in the air; bite: landed, fangs down; recover: flattened, harmless; dead: on its back, legs curled up.
# hang, hangwind (#483, D103): on the thread head down, drawn upright and mirrored about x 15|16, far legs in the lighter
# N; hangwind is the drop wind-up (legs drawn in, fangs spread). silk: the thread tile, 1x4 at the cell's top-left (the fang
# pale f with one g texel, the pale f0e2a8 the eyes had before #236), tiled down the thread at run time.
# Danger family (#236, 2026-11-20): dark crimson body 86101f, glowing eyes ff6b57, rose lights away from the hero's headband c22a24.
